# Root ignores for the portfolio fork.
#
# backend/.gitignore and frontend/.gitignore still apply inside their own
# directories and carry the detailed rules (target/, node_modules, dist,
# logs/, uploads/, .claude/*). This file only covers the gaps that exist at
# the parent level, where neither of those two files reaches.

## Secrets
# backend/.gitignore already ignores *.env (with !test.env) inside backend/.
# frontend/.gitignore has no .env rule at all — frontend/dist/.env is caught
# only incidentally by its `dist` entry, and frontend/public/.env is caught by
# nothing. Vite reads .env from the project root, not public/, so that file
# feeds no build; it is just copied verbatim into dist/ and served to every
# visitor. Ignore env files everywhere and let the backend's !test.env
# negation keep working in its own scope.
*.env
.env

## macOS
# Each service ignores its own .DS_Store; this catches one at the repo root.
.DS_Store

## Local tooling
# Same split the two services use: per-machine settings stay out, the portable
# run configuration is tracked.
.claude/*
!.claude/launch.json

## Assistant-facing context notes
# Orientation notes for a fresh assistant session, not portfolio material —
# and both carry the company GitLab URL, which has no place in a public
# repository. They stay on disk (MONTH3_CONTEXT.md is the Month 3 handoff);
# they just do not ship.
backend/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md
backend/genai-service/MONTH3_CONTEXT.md
